  "body": "Hey together\r\n\r\nI don't know if this is the correct place for my question but I will ask it anyway.\r\n\r\nAccording to [this site](https://notifications.spec.whatwg.org/#permission-model) there are three permission states: `default`, `denied` and `granted`. In Firefox the user can disabled notifications temporary and I would like to persent that state to the user. So basicly I want to differentiate between `denied` and something like `temporary_denied`.\r\n\r\nHow could this be achieved? Through a browser specific feature? Or even through change in the standard? Or anything else?\r\n\r\nEDIT: [Cross reference to stackoverflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/49490817/check-if-browser-notifications-are-temporary-disabled-in-firefox)",
